  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date the Department of the Treasury has recorded $4.7B in contract obligations across 6,785 awards, with an average award size of $694K. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Obligations fell 44.9% year over year. Looking back across full fiscal years, obligations were $9.6B in FY21, $9.3B in FY22, $10.3B in FY23, $9.3B in FY24, and $8.5B in FY25. The FY2026 to date total of $4.7B is smaller than each of those prior annual totals. Top spending categories in FY2026 to date include Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining at $1B and Other Computer Related Services at $914M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $434M. The top vendors in FY2026 to date are STONEX FINANCIAL LTD at $885M and ASAHI REFINING USA INC at $375M, with several other firms receiving between $80.5M and $188M. These figures reflect contract obligations recorded so far in the fiscal year and do not represent a completed annual total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Treasury contract spending changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 44.9% year over year. Full fiscal-year obligations were $9.6B in FY21, $9.3B in FY22, $10.3B in FY23, $9.3B in FY24, and $8.5B in FY25, compared with $4.7B in FY26 to date. The FY2026 to date total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure. Average award size in the current period is $694K across 6,785 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the largest product and supplier concentrations right now?",
        "body": "NAICS categories concentrated at the top include Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining at $1B and Other Computer Related Services at $914M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $434M. Vendors are concentrated as well, led by STONEX FINANCIAL LTD at $885M and ASAHI REFINING USA INC at $375M, with other top firms ranging from $80.5M to $188M. These figures reflect FY2026 to date obligations."
      }
